# Normalize everything to LF in the repository, regardless of what a given
# checkout's core.autocrlf does to the working tree. Windows' Git ships with
# core.autocrlf=true at the system level (Program Files/Git/etc/gitconfig),
# which converts LF -> CRLF on every checkout. Prettier's default output is
# LF, so a branch switch, cherry-pick, or reset repeatedly reintroduced CRLF
# into files Prettier had already normalized, showing up as a whitespace-only
# diff on the next `git status` with nothing actually changed. `eol=lf` pins
# the working-tree line ending for text files regardless of autocrlf.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: no line-ending conversion, ever.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
